# Sneak {3}{G} (CR 702.190a): Bot1 attacks with Ornithopter on turn 3 and, once Bot2 has not blocked, casts Michelangelo's
# Technique in the declare blockers step for {3}{G} (two Forests, Mox Emerald, Mox Pearl), returning the unblocked Ornithopter to
# its hand. A sorcery cast this way resolves as usual: Argothian Elder and Woodland Changeling are put onto the battlefield, but
# not attacking (only a permanent spell whose sneak cost was paid enters attacking, CR 702.190b), so Bot2 takes no combat damage
# at all and the two are untapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Ornithopter
Michelangelo's Technique
Island
Island
Argothian Elder
Woodland Changeling
Island x6
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
Bot1.Hand.Michelangelo's Technique.Cast(Ability: Sneak)
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Argothian Elder; Woodland Changeling)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Forest; Mox Emerald; Mox Pearl; Argothian Elder; Woodland Changeling
Bot1.Battlefield.Argothian Elder.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Woodland Changeling.Tapped = false
Bot1.Hand = Ornithopter; Island; Island
Bot1.Graveyard = Michelangelo's Technique
